I have reviewed the current implementation of the Purchase Order API. All the requested endpoints are already implemented in

PurchaseOrderController
and registered in

routes/api.php
under the PO module RBAC middleware.

API Endpoints Summary
Method Endpoint Description
GET /api/v1/purchase-orders List POs (with pagination & status/vendor filters)
GET /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id} View PO with full line items and relationships
POST /api/v1/purchase-orders Create a new PO (Starts as DRAFT)
PUT /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id} Update a DRAFT PO (recalculates totals)
PATCH /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id}/approve Approve a DRAFT PO to OPEN status
PATCH /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id}/cancel Cancel an OPEN or DRAFT PO
Curl Commands for Testing
Replace {TOKEN} with your valid JWT and {ID} with the actual PO ID. Ensure the IDs used in the JSON body (like vendor_id, material_id, etc.) exist in your database.

1. List Purchase Orders
   bash
   curl --location --request GET 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders?status=DRAFT&per_page=10' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json'
2. View Single Purchase Order
   bash
   curl --location --request GET 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders/{ID}' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json'
3. Create New Purchase Order (POST)
   bash
   curl --location --request POST 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json' \
   --data-raw '{
   "vendor_id": 1,
   "currency_id": 1,
   "po_date": "2024-03-11",
   "delivery_terms": "EXW",
   "payment_terms": "NET30",
   "credit_days": 30,
   "billing_address": "TechVyassa Office, Bangalore",
   "ship_to_address": "Main Warehouse, Mumbai",
   "line_items": [
   {
   "material_id": 1,
   "uom_id": 1,
   "ordered_qty": 100,
   "unit_price": 50.50,
   "discount_pct": 5,
   "gst_tax_id": 1,
   "material_description": "Raw Steel Rods"
   }
   ]
   }'
4. Update Draft Purchase Order (PUT)
   bash
   curl --location --request PUT 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders/{ID}' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json' \
   --data-raw '{
   "remarks": "Updated quantity and added a note",
   "line_items": [
   {
   "material_id": 1,
   "uom_id": 1,
   "ordered_qty": 150,
   "unit_price": 50.50,
   "discount_pct": 10,
   "gst_tax_id": 1
   }
   ]
   }'
5. Approve Purchase Order (PATCH)
   bash
   curl --location --request PATCH 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders/{ID}/approve' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json'
6. Cancel Purchase Order (PATCH)
   bash
   curl --location --request PATCH 'http://localhost/api/v1/purchase-orders/{ID}/cancel' \
   --header 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' \
   --header 'Accept: application/json'
